# Supabase (dev) — Playground agent guide

This workspace is wired to the **playground/dev Supabase** — a scratch instance,
**not production**. You can build apps end-to-end here: schema migrations, seed
data, and querying via the API.

## Environment variables (already set in your container)

| Var | Use | Put in a browser bundle? |
|-----|-----|--------------------------|
| `SUPABASE_URL` | REST/Auth/Storage base (`{{ playground_supabase_url }}`) | ✅ yes (frontend) |
| `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` | public client key; RLS protects the rows | ✅ yes (frontend) |
| `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` | **bypasses RLS** (full data access) | ❌ NEVER — server/CLI only |
| `SUPABASE_DB_URL` | direct Postgres, DDL-capable (migrations) | ❌ NEVER — server/CLI only |
| `SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET` | sign/verify tokens locally (debug) | ❌ NEVER |
| `SUPABASE_STUDIO_URL` | Studio UI ({{ playground_supabase_studio_url | default('n/a') }}, behind SSO) | n/a |

> ⚠️ `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`, `SUPABASE_DB_URL` and `SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET` grant
> full, RLS-bypassing access. They must NEVER land in a frontend bundle, a `pgN`
> app's client code, or a public repo. Client apps use ONLY `SUPABASE_URL` +
> `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` and rely on Row-Level Security.

## Migrations

Create a new migration (timestamped SQL file):

```bash
f="supabase/migrations/$(date +%Y%m%d%H%M%S)_my_change.sql"
$EDITOR "$f"      # write your CREATE TABLE / ALTER ... / policies
```

Apply all migrations to the dev DB, open a psql shell, or smoke-test everything:

```bash
./scripts/db-migrate    # apply pending migrations
./scripts/db-psql       # psql "$SUPABASE_DB_URL"  (interactive, or -c 'select 1')
./scripts/check         # tooling + env + DB + anon-REST smoke test
```

`db-migrate` applies each **new** migration file with `psql`, in one transaction
together with a `public.schema_migrations` ledger entry, so re-runs only apply files
that haven't run yet. (The `supabase` CLI is installed for other uses, but is NOT
used to push migrations here: it forces a TLS connection that the internal
self-hosted DB doesn't offer — `psql` with `sslmode=disable` works instead.)

## Using Supabase from a `pgN` app (browser)

**Preferred — same-origin, no CORS.** Every `pgN.{{ global_host }}` proxies
`{{ playground_supabase_same_origin_path }}/*` to Supabase on the app's **own**
origin, so the browser never makes a cross-origin request (no CORS preflight at all):

```js
import { createClient } from '@supabase/supabase-js'
// Base = this app's own origin + the mount prefix. supabase-js appends /rest/v1 etc.
const supabase = createClient(location.origin + '{{ playground_supabase_same_origin_path }}', SUPABASE_ANON_KEY)
// e.g. a query hits  <origin>{{ playground_supabase_same_origin_path }}/rest/v1/notes
```

Caddy strips the `{{ playground_supabase_same_origin_path }}` prefix and forwards to
the Supabase gateway (Kong key-auth + RLS enforce access); this prefix bypasses the
SSO gate, so the anon key alone is enough. Supabase already versions its endpoints
(`/rest/v1`, `/auth/v1`, …), so `{{ playground_supabase_same_origin_path }}` is just a
mount point, not an API version.

**Alternative — cross-origin absolute URL** (also works; Kong sends `Allow-Origin: *`):

```js
const supabase = createClient(SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY)   // https://supabase-api.{{ global_host }}
```

Both paths use ONLY the anon key; RLS protects the rows. Prefer the same-origin path
for browser apps — it needs no CORS and keeps everything on one host.

## Edge functions (self-hosted deploy path)

`supabase functions deploy` does NOT work here (it only targets the hosted cloud).
Instead, functions are plain files:

```bash
mkdir -p functions/myapp_task && $EDITOR functions/myapp_task/index.ts   # Deno.serve(...)
# NEW function: available immediately at $SUPABASE_URL/functions/v1/myapp_task
# EDITED function: shed the cached worker first:
playgroundctl functions reload
curl -sS "$SUPABASE_URL/functions/v1/myapp_task" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $SUPABASE_ANON_KEY" -d '{"name":"test"}'
```

See `functions/hello/index.ts` for the minimal shape. Calls require a valid JWT
(anon key works). The runtime sees this directory read-only; app-prefix your
function names like every other shared object. Same-origin from a pgN app:
`<origin>{{ playground_supabase_same_origin_path }}/functions/v1/<name>`.

## Security do / don't

- ✅ RLS **on** for every table; anon sees only what a policy explicitly allows.
- ✅ `service_role` / `SUPABASE_DB_URL` only in server code or these CLI scripts.
- ❌ never ship `service_role` or the DB URL to the client.
- ❌ don't operate production data here — this is a throwaway instance.

See `migrations/20260101000000_example_notes.sql` for the reference RLS pattern
(per-user rows: anon denied, each authenticated user sees only `owner = auth.uid()`).
